1. Verify Network Reachability
ping -c 3 8.8.8.8


Works → network is up

Fails → interface, route, or firewall issue

2. Check DNS Resolution
getent hosts google.com


If this fails but ping works → DNS problem, not network.

3. Inspect Listening Ports
ss -lntp


Used when:

App is “running”

But traffic can’t reach it

4. Test Remote Connectivity
curl -I http://service:8080


Confirms:

Network

Port

Application response

5. Packet Path Debug
traceroute google.com


Helps identify:

Where traffic is getting blocked

Firewall or routing failures

DevOps Insight

If DNS fails, everything fails — always check DNS early.
